🚽 Test case: a storage-class modifier on an alias use belongs to the
🚽 declaration, not the typedef alias itself.
🚽
🚽 The counter is `salty`, so it persists across calls and the output is a
🚽 direct count of how many times the body ran. This expected "2 4" until
🚽 interpreter_visit_function_call() stopped executing user-defined
🚽 functions during ast_accept()'s pre-visit: two calls, each run twice,
🚽 gave 1,2 then 3,4. One invocation each gives 1 and 2, which is what a
🚽 static counter incremented once per call should say.
lit rizz Count;

rizz next_count() {
    salty Count count = 0;
    count = count + 1;
    bussin count;
}

skibidi main {
    rizz first = next_count();
    rizz second = next_count();
    yapping("%d %d", first, second);
    bussin 0;
}
